  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The entrance has an arrival sheet, and the pickup desk can see it without leaving its station.\", \"decision\": \"How should a reader announce arrival?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nA helper gathers names from arriving readers and carries the arrival sheet to the pickup desk at regular intervals. The desk receives grouped arrival updates without a continuous line of introductions.\nThe pickup desk adds names to the arrival sheet after briefly greeting each reader. A short personal check records arrivals before readers move aside.\nReaders add their names to the arrival sheet, and the pickup desk calls them when their books are ready. Readers can wait away from the desk until called."
    }
  ],
